# BK-0010 monitor ROM, 100000-117777. Call names come from bk0010.ann.

code 100000 MONCLD ; power-on entry: jump to the cold start
head 100000 Power-on entry. The first two words, the jump to the cold start,
head 100000 double as the (unused) slots for EMT 0 and EMT 2.

ptrs 100004 43 EMTTAB
head 100004 EMT table: EMT n uses the word at 100000+n (EMT 4-110). EMT 52-110
head 100004 point into the ROM at 160000.

code 100112 EMTDSP
head 100112 EMT dispatcher: the EMT instruction's low byte is a byte offset into
head 100112 the table at 100000. The routine is called with JSR PC; the
head 100112 dispatcher returns to the program with RTI.


# From the commented disassembly of this ROM (017) by Boris F. Frolkin,
# 1990, put in machine-readable form with Yu. A. Zaltsman in 1991; the
# monitor itself is by M. I. Dyabin, 1983-85. monitor.zip from
# https://gid.pdp-11.net/sources.html (given to gid by Wesha). Its names
# and its routine descriptions, translated; checked against this ROM: 1998
# of its 1999 instructions are here at the addresses it gives (at 116514 it
# has BCC where this ROM has BCS).


head 100140 EMT 14: initialize the ROM's drivers and the system cells. Out: R0-R4
head 100140 destroyed.

code 100260 MONIT
head 100260 Monitor start: stack at 1000, initialize every driver, then call the ROM
head 100260 at 120000 (FOCAL or BASIC); if there is none, the bus error lands in
head 100260 VECT4.

code 100300 MON
head 100300 The monitor's command loop: prompt, read a command and run it.

code 100442 VECT4
head 100442 Bus error (no reply on the bus) or the STOP key: reset the stack and
head 100442 return to the monitor.

code 100460 TYPE
head 100460 Print a string. In: R3 = string, its first byte the length. Out: R3 =
head 100460 past the string; R0, R2 destroyed.

code 100472 NUM8
head 100472 Read an octal number from the keyboard into R5 (Enter at once gives 0).
head 100472 R0 destroyed.

code 100536 READMG
head 100536 Load a file from tape, asking for its name first. In: R5 = load address.
head 100536 R0-R3 destroyed.

code 100656 READTL
head 100656 Load a file from the serial line. In: R5 = load address. R0-R2
head 100656 destroyed.

name 100720 SOOB1
head 100720 Messages: SOOB1 "?", SOOB2 "ИМЯ? " (name?), SOOB3 "ОШИБКА" (error), each
head 100720 with its length first.

name 100724 SOOB2

name 100732 SOOB3

code 100742 EMT4
head 100742 EMT 4: initialize the keyboard driver. R0 destroyed.

head 101010 EMT 6: read a key. Out: R0 low byte = key code, high byte = 0.

code 101136 VECT60
head 101136 Keyboard interrupt (vector 60). Keys are handled in the interrupt
head 101136 itself; РУС, ЛАТ, УСТ and СБР.ТАБ.ПОЗ don't reach KEYEND.

code 101332 TABS
head 101332 Set or clear a tab stop.

code 101362 VEC274
head 101362 Keyboard interrupt with АР2 (vector 274). ПОВТ, ИНДСУ, БЛРЕД, ТАБ,
head 101362 АР2+digit and codes 232, 233, 235, 236 don't reach KEYEND.

code 101636 TABUL
head 101636 Count the spaces to the next tab stop.

head 101724 EMT 10: read a line from the keyboard. In: R1 = buffer, R2 low = length,
head 101724 R2 high = terminator. Out: R1 = past the line, R2 = count left.

head 102004 EMT 12: set function key N. In: R0 = N (1-10), R1 = its text, first byte
head 102004 the length. R0 destroyed.

code 102032 BEEPSL
head 102032 Update the service line, then go on.

code 102052 BEEP
head 102052 Beep, then read the keyboard.

code 102124 KEYEND
head 102124 End of a key's handling: call the user's extra routine (DOPROG) if set.

code 102160 PACKTB
head 102160 Pack a tab position. Out: R0 = bit mask, R1 = offset into the table.

head 102234 EMT 16: print the character in R0.

code 102370 SIMCUR
head 102370 Draw character R0 from the font table and move the cursor right.

code 102414 NOEXIT
head 102414 Keep the current character position on the screen, scrolling up or down
head 102414 if needed.

code 102566 SCRLTX
head 102566 Scroll the screen one text line up (R3 = 0) or down (R3 = 1). SCROLL in
head 102566 Frolkin's listing.

code 102746 SIMBOL
head 102746 Draw the character whose number in the font table is in R0.

code 103222 INVTCU
head 103222 Invert the text cursor (the current character position).

code 103310 OTRRED
head 103310 Editing codes 10, 22-37.

code 103544 KOD30
head 103544 Code 30: backspace (ЗАБОЙ).

code 103600 KOD26
head 103600 Code 26: close up the line from the right.

code 103700 KOD27
head 103700 Code 27: open up the line to the right.

code 103760 KOD23
head 103760 Code 23: close up the lines from below.

code 104020 KOD24
head 104020 Code 24: open up the lines below.

code 104066 LENMOV
head 104066 Count the lines to move, from the one under the cursor to the bottom of
head 104066 the screen.

code 104130 OTR0
head 104130 Control codes other than the editing ones (0-7, 11-21).

code 104236 CTRL
head 104236 With the show-control-codes flag (ИНДСУ) set, draw a control code
head 104236 instead of acting on it.

code 104244 CTRLIS
head 104244 Draw a control code.

code 104316 RET9

code 104320 OTR200
head 104320 Control codes 200-237.

code 104722 KOD214
head 104722 Code 214: extended memory mode (narrow screen) on or off.

code 104730 NOTRP
head 104730 Full-screen mode; also entered at initialization.

code 104770 K1

code 105054 K3

code 105074 KOD225
head 105074 Code 225: text graphics on or off.

code 105232 KOD231
head 105232 Code 231: clear the rest of the line.

code 105272 KOD233
head 105272 Code 233: color mode (32 or 64 characters a line) on or off.

code 105500 KOD235
head 105500 Code 235: invert the whole screen.

code 105564 KODIS
head 105564 Draw a control code's picture while editing is blocked.

code 105670 EMT16G
head 105670 EMT 16 in graphics mode (ГРАФ).

code 105744 MOVEGK
head 105744 Move the graphics cursor.

code 106234 STEPG
head 106234 Move to the next graphics point: R1 = dx, R2 = dy.

code 106536 ADRG
head 106536 Work out the address of the byte holding the current point (the source's
head 106536 marker says 106530).

code 106564 INVGCU
head 106564 Invert the graphics cursor.

code 106772 NEXTW
head 106772 Move to the next word on the right.

code 107012 SBOR10
head 107012 Collect a decimal repeat count for the next direction code into VECLEN.

head 107050 EMT 20: print a string. In: R1 = string, R2 low = length, R2 high =
head 107050 terminator. Out: R1 = past the string, R2 = count left.

head 107106 EMT 22: put a character in the service line. In: R0 = code (0 clears the
head 107106 line), R1 = position (0-63).

code 107200 SIMSLU
head 107200 Draw a character in the service line.

head 107272 EMT 24: move the cursor. In: R1 = X (text 0-63, graphics 0-511; half in
head 107272 color mode), R2 = Y (text 0-23, graphics 0-239; text 0-3 in extended
head 107272 memory mode).

head 107502 EMT 26: read the text or graphics cursor's position. Out: R1 = X, R2 = Y
head 107502 (ranges as for EMT 24).

head 107612 EMT 30: draw (R0 = 1) or erase (R0 = 0) the point R1 = X (0-511; 0-255
head 107612 in color), R2 = Y (0-239).

code 107626 PIXEL
head 107626 Draw a point: R1 = X, R2 = Y, R0 = draw (1) or erase (0).

head 107776 EMT 32: draw (R0 = 1) or erase (R0 = 0) a line from the last point to R1
head 107776 = X, R2 = Y.

code 110270 LINE
head 110270 Draw a straight run of R4 points.

head 110310 EMT 34: the display's status word. Out: R0 bits 0-15 = the mode flags in
head 110310 bytes 40-57 (zero or not).

code 110340 SAVESY
head 110340 Reset the system register and push R4-R0. Called with JSR R4,SAVESY.

code 110346 SAVE
head 110346 Push R4-R0. Called with JSR R4,SAVE.

code 110362 REST
head 110362 Pop R0-R4 pushed by SAVE or SAVESY. Called with JSR R4,REST.

code 110376 CLRSCR
head 110376 Clear the whole screen.

code 110442 MOVG00
head 110442 Put the graphics cursor in the top left corner.

code 110470 SLUSTR
head 110470 Redraw the whole service line.

code 110536 SLUIND
head 110536 Update every indicator in the service line.

code 110572 TYPESL
head 110572 Draw one mode indicator in the service line: R0 = 0 РУС/ЛАТ, 1
head 110572 underline, 2 inverse, 3 ИНДСУ, 4 БЛРЕД, 5 ГРАФ/ЗАП/СТИР.

code 111130 TYPETB
head 111130 Mark the tab stops in the service line.

code 111314 INVCUR
head 111314 Invert the cursor.

code 111352 MOVCUR
head 111352 Move the text cursor to the new SIMADR, already set.

code 111374 CLRCUR
head 111374 Clear the character position under the cursor.

code 111434 NEXT
head 111434 The address of the byte one raster line down.

code 111450 FULLUP
head 111450 Fill a screen line upwards, -(R3), with the word R1.

code 111474 FULLDN
head 111474 Fill a screen line downwards, (R3)+, with the word R1.

code 111516 MOVEUP
head 111516 Move R2 raster lines at (R1) one text line up.

code 111616 MOVEDN
head 111616 Move R2 raster lines at (R1) one text line down.

name 111734 INDLAT
head 111734 Service-line indicator labels (" ЛАТ", " РУС", "ПОДЧ", "ИНВ ", "ИСУ ",
head 111734 "БЛР ", "ГРАФ", "ЗАП ", "СТИР"), as character numbers in the font table.

name 111740 INDRUS

name 111744 INDPOD

name 111750 INDINW

name 111754 INDISU

name 111760 INDBLR

name 111764 INDGRA

name 111770 INDZAP

name 111774 INDSTI

name 112000 IND

name 112004 MASPOZ
head 112004 Position masks.

name 112026 CWET
head 112026 The four colors' masks.

name 112036 TABLE
head 112036 Character images (the font), 10 bytes each.

head 116076 EMT 36: tape. In: R1 = parameter block (320). Out: the result byte
head 116076 (321), MASADR (264) and MASLEN (266) = address and length of the file
head 116076 loaded, MWOZ (301) = return code.

code 116214 VEC4MG
head 116214 The STOP key during a tape operation.

code 116232 OKOMAG
head 116232 End of a tape operation.

code 116256 MAGWR
head 116256 Write a file to tape.

code 116404 SINMAR
head 116404 Write a pilot of R0 periods (R4, R5 adjust the first), then the marker
head 116404 and its post-bit. R3 = 177716; R1, R2 kept.

code 116474 OUTBTS
head 116474 Write 8 sync bits: time for the reader to compare the header (Frolkin:
head 116474 too little to print the name too).

code 116504 OUTBT
head 116504 Write R2 bytes from (R1)+ to tape.

code 116512 O

code 116516 OUT0
head 116516 Write a 0 bit.

code 116544 OUT1
head 116544 Write a 1 bit.

code 116570 OUTSIN
head 116570 Write a sync bit (the same as a 0).

code 116622 KONSUM
head 116622 Checksum of an array. In: R5 = address, R4 = length in bytes. Out: R0 =
head 116622 the sum.

code 116640 MAGRD
head 116640 Read a file from tape.

code 116656 I

code 116712 ISKSIN
head 116712 Find a file's pilot and measure it.

code 117062 I2
head 117062 Read error: start again from the pilot search.

code 117064 I1

code 117070 INGOL
head 117070 Read a file's header and compare its name with the one wanted.

code 117154 INMASS
head 117154 Read the file's data.

code 117260 INBTS
head 117260 Read an array of bytes, skipping the sync bits first.

code 117336 INBT
head 117336 Read R2 bytes to (R1)+, stepping by MDELTA.

code 117376 PERIOD
head 117376 Measure the next bit's period into R4, after skipping a sync bit.

code 117462 EMT40
head 117462 EMT 40: set the serial line's speed. In: R0 = 0 9600 baud, 1 4800, 2
head 117462 2400, 3 1200, 4 600, 5 300, 6 150, 7 75, 10 50.

code 117474 EMT42
head 117474 EMT 42: send the byte in R0 on the serial line.

code 117566 EMT44
head 117566 EMT 44: receive a byte from the serial line into R0.

code 117704 EMT46
head 117704 EMT 46: send R2 bytes from R1 on the serial line. Out: R1 += R2, R2 = 0.

code 117722 EMT50
head 117722 EMT 50: receive R2 bytes to R1 from the serial line. Out: R1 += R2, R2 =
head 117722 0.

name 117740 SPEED
head 117740 Serial line speed constants.
